---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Production Planning & Scheduling" description="A constraint-aware daily and weekly production planning system that reduced routine planning work from hours to minutes.">
<section class="case-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="case-back" href={`${base}/built-systems/`}>← Built Systems</a>
    <div class="case-kicker">06 / Production Planning</div>
    <h1>Production Planning<br/><em>& Scheduling</em></h1>
    <p class="case-deck">A constraint-aware planning system that turns current work-in-process into practical daily and weekly execution priorities.</p>
    <div class="case-role-line"><span>Workflow Redesign</span><span>Business Logic</span><span>Capacity Planning</span><span>AI-Assisted Development</span><span>Validation</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-metrics case-metrics-dark">
  <div class="container case-metric-grid">
    <div><strong>~13–19 hrs</strong><span>My Previous Weekly Planning Time</span></div>
    <div><strong>~5–10 min</strong><span>Current Daily Planning Time</span></div>
    <div><strong>7–8</strong><span>Departments Impacted</span></div>
    <div><strong>~200</strong><span>Employees' Work Priorities Affected</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="container case-two-col">
    <div><div class="case-section-no">01</div><div class="eyebrow">The Constraint</div>
      <h2>A daily production plan could take hours to build and become obsolete almost immediately.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-copy">
      <p>The facility's legacy planning software required supervisors to manually enter and manage work orders across multiple operations, repeatedly include or exclude routing steps, and update plans throughout the day when work did not move as expected.</p>
      <p>For me, the process typically consumed four to six hours on Monday, two to three hours on most midweek days, and another three to four hours on Friday to plan ahead. The software was also unstable and did not account cleanly for staffing capacity, expected operation spans, or several constraints supervisors managed manually.</p>
      <p class="case-emphasis">I replaced the repeated manual planning work with a refreshable model: paste current WIP, run the planner, review feasibility, and adjust only where judgment is needed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt scheduler-architecture-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">02</div><div class="eyebrow">Planning Architecture</div>
    <h2>One master schedule, with each layer doing one job.</h2>
    <div class="scheduler-architecture">
      <div class="arch-source"><small>INPUT</small><strong>Current WIP</strong><span>WO · Part · Current operation · Qty · TOC</span></div>
      <div class="arch-source"><small>INPUT</small><strong>Routing</strong><span>Sequence · WC · ESH / Plan hrs · Span</span></div>
      <div class="arch-source"><small>CONTROL</small><strong>Settings</strong><span>Capacity · Horizon · Throughput target · Buffers</span></div>

      <div class="arch-stage"><small>01</small><strong>Route Interpretation</strong><span>What remains?</span></div>
      <div class="arch-stage"><small>02</small><strong>Throughput Leveling</strong><span>When do we want the credit?</span></div>
      <div class="arch-stage"><small>03</small><strong>Capacity Allocation</strong><span>When can the work physically fit?</span></div>

      <div class="arch-master"><small>MASTER RESULT SET</small><strong>Weekly Operations</strong><span>One operation-level schedule consumed by every downstream view</span></div>

      <div class="arch-output"><strong>Weekly Summary</strong><span>Plan + throughput</span></div>
      <div class="arch-output"><strong>Weekly Load</strong><span>WC/day capacity</span></div>
      <div class="arch-output"><strong>Pipeline</strong><span>Incoming work</span></div>
      <div class="arch-output"><strong>External Returns</strong><span>Span-driven timing</span></div>
      <div class="arch-output"><strong>ESH</strong><span>Plan measurement</span></div>
      <div class="arch-output"><strong>Daily Dispatcher</strong><span>Separate execution-priority engine</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section scheduler-exception-section">
  <div class="container route-example">
    <div><div class="case-section-no">03</div><div class="eyebrow">Exception Logic</div>
      <h2>The schedule understands that work can leave the department and still belong to the plan.</h2>
      <p>Routing spans are encoded so work orders temporarily disappear from actionable work while they are expected elsewhere, then return to the schedule when that external span should be complete.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-flow">
      <div><small>Monday</small><strong>Current Operation</strong></div><b>→</b>
      <div class="route-away"><small>2-Day Span</small><strong>External Process</strong></div><b>→</b>
      <div><small>Thursday</small><strong>Expected Return</strong></div><b>→</b>
      <div class="route-late"><small>If Missing</small><strong>Flag Late</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt scheduler-human-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">04</div><div class="eyebrow">Human in the Loop</div>
    <h2>Automate the planning load, not the supervisor's judgment.</h2>
    <div class="human-loop">
      <div><strong>01</strong><span>Paste current work orders</span></div><b>→</b>
      <div><strong>02</strong><span>Run the macro</span></div><b>→</b>
      <div><strong>03</strong><span>Review feasibility</span></div><b>→</b>
      <div><strong>04</strong><span>Make quick WIP swaps if needed</span></div><b>→</b>
      <div><strong>05</strong><span>Publish the plan</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">Formula, formatting, prioritization, and VBA implementation were developed with AI assistance. I defined the operational parameters, work-center scope, routing behavior, span logic, constraints, planning goals, and validation criteria.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section scheduler-impact-section">
  <div class="container current-state-grid">
    <div><div class="case-section-no">05</div><div class="eyebrow">Observed Impact</div><h2>Planning moved from a recurring time sink to a short review process.</h2>
      <p>My routine planning work dropped from approximately 13–19 hours per week to roughly 5–10 minutes per day under normal conditions. The system also makes aged inventory, late returns, expected throughput, and missed assignments easier to see.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="roadmap"><div class="eyebrow">Next Iteration</div><span>Attendance Feed</span><span>Workforce Capability Integration</span><span>Automated Alerts</span><span>More Direct Production-System Inputs</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-artifact-section scheduler-artifacts">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="artifact-head">
      <div><div class="case-section-no">06</div><div class="eyebrow">Reconstructed Views</div><h2>The original workbook is proprietary. The operating logic is documented.</h2></div>
      <div class="artifact-reconstruction-copy">
        <p>These portfolio views are reconstructed from the scheduler's documented architecture using synthetic work orders. They show the structure of the system without reproducing production data.</p>
        <div class="scheduler-capabilities"><span>Sequence-Aware Routing</span><span>Split Operations</span><span>External Spans</span><span>Defined Throughput Credit</span></div>
        <div class="technical-brief-cta">
          <a class="technical-overview-link" href="/downloads/production-planning-scheduling-technical-brief.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the Technical Overview <span>→</span></a>
          <p>Architecture, scheduling logic, exception handling, controls, and implementation details.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="scheduler-view scheduler-view-large">
      <div class="scheduler-window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Weekly Operations — Master Schedule</b></div>
      <div class="scheduler-window-body">
        <div class="sched-head"><span>WO</span><span>Part</span><span>Operation</span><span>Work Center</span><span>Mon</span><span>Tue</span><span>Wed</span><span>Thu</span><span>Fri</span><span>Credit</span></div>
        <div class="sched-row"><strong>WO-2604</strong><span>PX-104</span><span>010</span><span>Finish A</span><i class="work">3.0h</i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><b></b></div>
        <div class="sched-row"><strong>WO-2604</strong><span>PX-104</span><span>020</span><span>Prep A</span><i></i><i class="work">2.0h</i><i></i><i></i><i></i><b></b></div>
        <div class="sched-row"><strong>WO-2604</strong><span>PX-104</span><span>030</span><span>Finish A</span><i></i><i class="work">3.0h</i><i></i><i></i><i></i><b></b></div>
        <div class="sched-row"><strong>WO-2604</strong><span>PX-104</span><span>040</span><span>Credit</span><i></i><i></i><i class="credit">1.5h</i><i></i><i></i><b>$73K</b></div>
        <div class="sched-row"><strong>WO-2602</strong><span>PX-102</span><span>020</span><span>External</span><i></i><i class="span">2-day span</i><i class="span"></i><i></i><i></i><b></b></div>
        <div class="sched-row"><strong>WO-2607</strong><span>PX-107</span><span>010</span><span>Finish A</span><i class="work">7.0h</i><i class="work">1.5h</i><i></i><i></i><i></i><b></b></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="scheduler-view-grid">
      <div class="scheduler-view">
        <div class="scheduler-window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Daily Dispatcher</b></div>
        <div class="scheduler-window-body compact">
          <div class="dispatcher-head"><span>Priority</span><span>WO</span><span>WC</span><span>Need Today</span></div>
          <div class="dispatcher-row"><b>01</b><strong>WO-2607</strong><span>Finish A</span><em>Complete split op</em></div>
          <div class="dispatcher-row"><b>02</b><strong>WO-2604</strong><span>Prep A</span><em>Route progression</em></div>
          <div class="dispatcher-row"><b>03</b><strong>WO-2614</strong><span>Inspect</span><em>Credit ready</em></div>
          <div class="dispatcher-row"><b>04</b><strong>WO-2605</strong><span>Prep B</span><em>Capacity fallback</em></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scheduler-view">
        <div class="scheduler-window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Weekly Load</b></div>
        <div class="scheduler-window-body compact">
          <div class="load-head"><span>WC</span><span>Mon</span><span>Tue</span><span>Wed</span><span>Thu</span><span>Fri</span></div>
          <div class="load-row"><strong>Prep A</strong><i class="med">72%</i><i class="high">94%</i><i class="low">43%</i><i class="med">68%</i><i class="low">31%</i></div>
          <div class="load-row"><strong>Finish A</strong><i class="high">100%</i><i class="high">96%</i><i class="med">74%</i><i class="med">61%</i><i class="low">28%</i></div>
          <div class="load-row"><strong>Inspect</strong><i class="med">64%</i><i class="low">38%</i><i class="high">91%</i><i class="med">70%</i><i class="low">35%</i></div>
          <div class="load-row"><strong>Credit</strong><i class="low">32%</i><i class="med">58%</i><i class="med">76%</i><i class="high">88%</i><i class="med">55%</i></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="scheduler-view-grid second">
      <div class="scheduler-view">
        <div class="scheduler-window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Weekly Summary</b></div>
        <div class="scheduler-window-body compact centered">
          <div class="summary-kpis"><div><span>MON</span><strong>$286K</strong></div><div><span>TUE</span><strong>$304K</strong></div><div><span>WED</span><strong>$297K</strong></div><div><span>THU</span><strong>$309K</strong></div><div><span>FRI</span><strong>$291K</strong></div></div>
          <div class="throughput-line"><span>Target band</span><i></i><b>$280K–$310K / day</b></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scheduler-view">
        <div class="scheduler-window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Exceptions & Returns</b></div>
        <div class="scheduler-window-body compact">
          <div class="exception-row"><b>RETURN</b><span>WO-2602</span><strong>Expected Thu</strong></div>
          <div class="exception-row"><b>ROUTE</b><span>WO-2620</span><strong>Missing route</strong></div>
          <div class="exception-row"><b>CAPACITY</b><span>WO-2607</span><strong>Operation split</strong></div>
          <div class="exception-row"><b>ESH</b><span>WO-2605</span><strong>PLAN hrs fallback</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="case-note scheduler-reconstruction-note"><strong>Reconstruction note:</strong> the original system used modular VBA, including separate routing, leveling, capacity, weekly, daily-dispatch, pipeline, ESH, output, and orchestration modules. The portfolio visuals above reproduce the documented architecture and decision logic, not the original production workbook.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-next"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Related System</span>
  <a href={`${base}/built-systems/workforce-capability-planning/`}><strong>Workforce Capability Planning System</strong><span>→</span></a>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
